sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Client / SDK
    participant E as EvalHub API / runtime
    participant R as TrustyAI reconciler
    participant P as Platform sandbox service
    participant G as OpenShell gateway / driver
    participant K as Guardrails / K8s controllers
    participant S as Primary evaluator sandbox
    participant B as Trusted per-attempt broker
    participant C as Child sandbox
    participant X as Trusted integration relay

    U->>E: Submit evaluation with provider / collection
    E->>E: Authorize tenant and resolve required profiles and capabilities
    alt Mandatory sandbox or required capability unavailable
        E-->>U: Descriptive error, no plain Job fallback
    else Preflight passes
        E->>E: Persist evaluation and durable dispatch intent
        E->>R: Create versioned SandboxedEvaluation (idempotent)
        E-->>U: Evaluation ID through existing asynchronous API
        R->>P: Ensure attempt (tenant UID, profiles, envelope, deadline)
        P->>P: Obtain aggregate / Kueue admission where enabled
        P->>G: Ensure ephemeral workspace, templates, providers, membership
        Note over P,B: Unique workspace-user identity per attempt, broker outside sandbox
        P->>B: Deliver only this attempt's gateway identity
        R->>B: Provision bounded endpoint and attempt capability
        P->>G: Ensure primary sandbox using complete approved profile
        G->>K: Prepare managed namespace and sandbox resources
        K->>K: SCC allocation, quota, limits, PSA, effective policy, storage
        Note over G,K: Required platform extension: deny execution until guardrails ready
        K-->>G: Attest readiness and release approved execution
        G->>S: Start sandbox runtime / evaluator
        G-->>R: Workspace, namespace UID and sandbox ready
        R->>E: Mirror benchmark Running and provenance
        loop Each qualified child request within declared limits
            S->>B: Kubernetes-shaped create (attempt authentication)
            B->>B: Bind caller and validate kind, image, fan-out, depth, TTL
            B->>G: Create child with pinned policy and provider bindings
            G->>G: Independently authorize workspace and effective profile
            G->>K: Reconcile approved child workload and supervisor
            K->>C: Start child sandbox
            G-->>B: Child sandbox ID and state
            B-->>S: Logical Pod-compatible result
            S->>B: exec / log / attach
            B->>G: Qualified remote-execution / stream operation
            G->>C: Supervisor-mediated command / observation
            C-->>G: Output, stream state and exit status
            G-->>B: Stream / exit status
            B-->>S: Qualified Kubernetes-compatible stream
        end
        S->>X: Job-bound events and result artifacts
        X->>E: Authorized tenant / evaluation / benchmark update
        alt Completion or failure
            R->>R: Record execution outcome and freeze child spawning
        else Cancel request or absolute deadline
            U->>E: Cancel evaluation (or deadline fires)
            E->>R: Reconcile cancellation / deadline
        end
        R->>B: Revoke capability, reject creates and close streams
        R->>P: Terminate attempt compute and export available results
        P->>G: Stop primary and all child sandboxes, retain output storage
        G->>K: Terminate workloads and supervisors
        R->>X: Finalize staged artifacts / qualified trusted storage export
        X-->>R: Export state / retained artifact references
        alt Required export complete or authorized data disposition
            P->>G: Remove sandboxes, storage, templates, providers, services, settings
            P->>G: Remove membership and delete workspace
            G->>K: Delete managed namespace and owned resources
            K-->>P: Verify namespace UID / PVC / volume cleanup
            P->>P: Revoke attempt identity and release capacity after termination
            alt Cleanup verified
                P-->>R: CleanupComplete plus audit / deletion evidence
                R->>E: Final outcome + export / cleanup provenance
                R->>R: Remove finalizer
            else Outage or stuck deletion
                P-->>R: CleanupBlocked with retained resource IDs
                R->>R: Retry, alert and record durable orphan responsibility
            end
        else Required export blocked
            R->>P: Revoke identity and retain protected output for bounded recovery
            R->>E: Results failure and visible cleanup / retention state
        end
        Note over R,K: Platform TTL sweeper recovers after crashes, timeout is not cleanup success
    end
